Ben,
After experimenting with the ratio jumpers, it appears that the base clock
is 50Mhz. This correclates with the manual stating that the default ratio is
2/1 for 100Mhz cpu's.
I also can not find a clock jumper. So I once again come to the issue of J4.
It is situated towards the top right corner of the main board and is made up
of an array of 12 or so pins with about 4 jumpers. It is close to where the
OPC cable plugs in.
I am now rerunning memory tests with only 1 cpu, to see if I can get a
conssitent result, but I am worried that the randomness of the failures is
in itself a clue.
I will check power supply rails next.
By the way, the user manual table for J3,J4,J7,J8 appears to be correct, but
J3 and J4 are silk screened in swapped positions on the cpu module.
Therefore the silkscreen table on the bottom corner of the cpu module is
also incorrect.

Thanks,
Doc

