yeah, the dec3000s were really great machines. they continued the tradition
of the DECstations of being totally indestructible, unstoppable machines, and
they were way fast for the time. I still have one 3000/600 running 24/7
and it has been for years, never a trouble, and it still can hold its own
at everyday tasks. They do suck down a lot of power, though.. the
only downside to them, i'd say. I used to have a rack with 7 3000/400s
in it, all humming away running netbsd in a beowulf cluster.. that thing
blew a very warm breeze out the exhaust side of the machines, if you stood
on that side (the side panel had been removed to get rid of the hot air),
you were much warmer than the rest of the machine room.. :-)
yeah, i gave six of that 7 away last year and 4 of them were taken by
two guys who drove almost 600 miles for them!

