> Can anyone tell me the differences between the DEC Personal
> Workstation PWS Alpha 600a and the 600au?

Yes.

> It would appear the 600a shipped with NT and the 600au Tru64 UNIX and
> that the 600a had an ide controller too. But is there any reason the
> 600a can't be used with Tru64 UNIX?

The basic hardware is the same, but in the 600a-Version are in most cases
Adaptec SCSI-Controllers and Matrox graphics cards and in the 600au are
QLogic SCSI-Controllers and PowerStorm graphics card and in the old
au-Version
(Miata MX5) a SCSI-CD-ROM.

Tru64 UNIX cannot work neither work with the Adaptec nor with the Matrox
card.
You need to replace this cards and switch from AlphaBIOS to SRM. Then you
can
run Tru64. If you want to run OpenVMS you also should replace the IDE-CD-ROM
with a SCSI-CD-ROM.




