Doc,

Yes, if you have a matched set of 4 P200s, you can transform the computer into
an HX5200MP/4.

The correct settings according to DEC documents are:

3/2 - J3, J4, J7, J8 OFF
2/1 - J3 OFF, J4 ON, J7 OFF, J8 ON
5/2 - J3, J4, J7, J8 ON
3/1 - J3 ON, J4 OFF, J7 ON, J8 OFF

The manual is logically consistent.

The front-side bus on these beasts is apparently locked at 66MHz.  Or, to be
more accurate, there does not appear to be a jumper to set the front side bus
clock to a speed anything other than 66MHz.  With P100s currently installed, the
bus has to be 66MHz anyway, so you only need to change the clock multiplier
settings... Ben Myers 

