RZ25 Hard Disk Drive install in Macintosh SE/30

Warning:  Hazardous voltages can exist inside a compact Macintosh.
The video tube can act as a very large capacitor, even if the
system is unplugged.  Be careful when using power tools.

Disclaimer:  These were my results, your mileage may vary.

Background:  I wanted to upgrade the disk and memory capacity
of a Mac SE/30.  This would make it possible to install and run
NetBSD, which would make the system more useful for my purposes.
My budget for this project was small, so I planned to use a Digital
RZ25 disk salvaged from a dead Alpha workstation.

Spinup:  As installed in the Alpha, the RZ25 does not spin up on
power-up.  A search of Google groups for the words "RZ25 jumper"
turned up several posts with consistent information on the jumpers
for this drive.  Spinup behavior is controlled by jumper P2 in jumper
block J6.  Removing J6/P2 caused the drive to spin up on power-up.
(Note:  I orginally removed the incorrect jumber instead.  The
only operation from the Macintosh which caused the drive to
spin up for me was to access it with the Lido disk formatter.
See http://www.euronet.nl/users/ernstoud/lido7.html.  I'm
aware of SCSIprobe, but the version I tried would not run
on my SE30.)

SCSI termination:  To access the RZ25 as an external drive,
I needed to install jumper J6/P7 (Drive supplies power to
SCSI bus), remove jumper J6/P8 (Power to internal terminators),
and use an external terminator with a green LED labeled 'Falcon'
(the vendor name) and 'Active'.  To access the RZ25 as an
internal drive (mounted inside the Mac) I found that I needed to
install jumper J6/P7, remove jumber J6/P8, and use a passive
terminator that fit between the 50-pin cable and the hard drive.

Physical mounting:  The RZ25 mounting holes do not match the
location of the holes for the original Quantum 40MB drive.  I 
removed the bracket and drilled new holes in the bracket which 
allowed me to mount the drive.

Formatting and Partitioning:  I used a patched version of
Apple's HD SC Setup 7.3.5 as describe here:  
http://www.euronet.nl/users/ernstoud/patch.html
This worked well for me.


