The service manual doesn't mention 0008.0280, only 0008.000F =
"Operating system error" or "System software error" (according to
which page of the manual you read), but doesn't explain that further.

It says 00400000 means you have only 4Mb of memory, which is strange,
unless it gives up after finding the onboard memory faulty (which is
what 0000000x means -- 000000y0 would mean a fault in the expansion
memory).

