Chris Ball <cjb@earthquake.boredom.org> writes in article <slrnb672j1.ke5.cjb@earthquake.boredom.org> dated Mon, 03 Mar 2003 17:01:21 +0000:
>   >>>show device;
>   dva.0.0.0.0.1        DVA0
>
>I'd expect both the HDD and CD-ROM to show up there.

Yes they should.  I think the masters show up as dqa0 and dqb0, the slaves
as dqa1 and dqb1.  

>The IDE controller is on the PCI-ISA bridge and listed in `show config`:
>
>   PCI: Slot 11: CMD PC10646 IDE Controller dqa.0.0.11.0
>
>Are there any known problems with booting IDE through SRM on this model?
>What's the relevance of the 'dqa..' listing in show config?

If "show config" is reading info from the actual system (as opposed to 
regurgitating saved data), it means that the controller is at least still
talking to the system.  Check the IDE cable(s) to make sure they're
plugged in solidly.  

If there are 2 devices on each cable try just 1 -- first the master and if
that doesn't work try the slave device, but promote it to master with the
appropriate jumper.  The theory here is that one drive could be screwing up
the bus for the other 2 devices (the controller and the other drive).

>I've (just today) upgraded the SRM console from ftp.digital.com's
>/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/archive/alphapc164/ .  The v5.5-1 string is
>still being shown on boot, though, and the site tells me that I was 
>flashing to v5.6.

On some models you need to cycle the system power to get the new SRM.

I'm assuming the problem was present before you upgraded?  If not, go back
to the old firmware!

--Keith Lewis              klewis$mitre.org
