Very old printers.

Anyhow, probably what has happened is the pickups rollers are becoming hard.

This is going to seem like a lot of work, it is. I have done this job to a
number of printer over the years including Epsons and H-P's and it can be
worth it.

1. Disassemble printer.
2. Remove the rubber compound rollers from their mounts.
3. Wash with soap and rinse well, all the rollers. Dry carefully. No alcohol
of any kind.
4. Lightly scuff the surface with a 300 grit sandpaper, the grey stuff with
clothe back. Probably you will need to make 6 to 8 swipes evenly across the
entire surface of the rubber rollers.
5. Reassemble printers and enjoy another bunch of years use.

rtt




